# The pad's menu keys, which hold only while the menus are up and the pad has their cursor: Back and B are Escape,
# Start is Enter, A is a left click (under the cursor shown when that is on a control, else on the focused control
# when that takes a click) or Enter, the D-pad is the arrow keys and an arrow the focused control does not use moves
# the focus as Tab does (down and right to the next control, up and left to the previous one). In play the buttons
# are their Joy keys and their bindings (DefUser.ini: Back shows the scores, Start opens the menus). Start a map,
# e.g. 'DM-Deck16][?Game=Botpack.DeathMatchPlus'.
waitlog up for play
sleep 3
pad attach
sleep 1
pad button a 1
pad button a 0
pad button b 1
pad button b 0
pad button dpup 1
pad button dpup 0
pad button back 1
pad button back 0
sleep 0.5
probe play
# Start's binding opens the menus with the Game menu dropped down; the mouse then takes the cursor out of the way.
pad button start 1
pad button start 0
sleep 1
probe menus
mouse 400 400
sleep 0.3
probe mouse-has-it
# A press takes the cursor back and acts: Right twice goes to Options, Down to Preferences, and A, with the cursor
# on no control, is Enter and runs it.
pad button dpright 1
pad button dpright 0
sleep 0.3
probe right-1
pad button dpright 1
pad button dpright 0
sleep 0.3
probe right-2
pad button dpdown 1
pad button dpdown 0
sleep 0.3
probe down
pad button a 1
pad button a 0
sleep 1
probe a-enter
# With the cursor off the window, A clicks the focused control: the checkbox toggles (twice, back as it was), and
# once the D-pad has moved the focus to the drop-down below it, A opens its list and B closes it.
mouse 600 450
sleep 0.3
probe focus-checkbox
pad button a 1
pad button a 0
sleep 0.3
probe a-toggles
pad button a 1
pad button a 0
sleep 0.3
probe a-toggles-back
# In the Preferences window the D-pad's down and up move the focus from control to control.
pad button dpdown 1
pad button dpdown 0
sleep 0.3
probe focus-1
pad button a 1
pad button a 0
sleep 0.3
probe a-opens-list
pad button b 1
pad button b 0
sleep 0.3
probe b-closes-list
pad button dpdown 1
pad button dpdown 0
sleep 0.3
probe focus-2
pad button dpdown 1
pad button dpdown 0
sleep 0.3
probe focus-3
pad button dpup 1
pad button dpup 0
sleep 0.3
probe focus-back
# The texture detail drop-down: A opens it, the D-pad selects in it and A picks: first Medium (up to the top, High,
# then down one), then High, which UT99 asks to confirm in a message box. Its buttons take no keyboard focus and it
# takes no Enter: the cursor and A answer it, or B closes it as the keyboard's Escape does (the value stays Medium).
pad button dpdown 1
pad button dpdown 0
sleep 0.3
probe texture-detail
pad button a 1
pad button a 0
sleep 0.3
pad button dpup 1
pad button dpup 0
pad button dpup 1
pad button dpup 0
pad button dpup 1
pad button dpup 0
pad button dpdown 1
pad button dpdown 0
sleep 0.2
pad button a 1
pad button a 0
sleep 0.5
probe picked-medium
pad button a 1
pad button a 0
sleep 0.3
pad button dpup 1
pad button dpup 0
sleep 0.2
pad button a 1
pad button a 0
sleep 0.5
probe picked-high
pad button b 1
pad button b 0
sleep 0.5
probe box-closed
# B closes the window, Back the menus.
pad button b 1
pad button b 0
sleep 0.5
probe b
pad button back 1
pad button back 0
sleep 1
probe back
# A with the cursor shown on a control clicks it: the cursor on Options in the menu bar drops its menu down.
pad button start 1
pad button start 0
sleep 1
mouse 100 5
sleep 0.2
pad axis leftx 6000
sleep 0.05
pad axis leftx 0
sleep 0.3
pad button a 1
pad button a 0
sleep 0.5
probe a-click
